-- title:
--   Local regularity of Gauss-integral functions integral over ℚ̄[j]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, a nonzero level $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, a modular polynomial datum `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi_q \equiv (Y^q - X)(Y - X^q) \pmod q$, and the hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ that the two degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` of the level-$N$ into the level-$Nq$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ are integral; let $P$ be a specialisation packet `PlaceSpecialization` for these data and assume $q \nmid N$. Let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$ and let $Q$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is strict of the first kind, i.e. the geometric-level Frobenius carries the first reduction $\bar v =$ `P.reduceFst Q` to the second reduction `P.reduceSnd Q` and its square does not fix $\bar v$. Assume further: some pair $c \in k \times k$ is a centre of $\bar v$ (both $j - c_1$ and $j_N - c_2$, in the geometric generators `jGeomGen`, `jNGeomGen`, have positive order at $\bar v$) and is the centre of no other place of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`; the value of `jNGeomGen k N` at $\bar v$ is not fixed by raising to the $q^2$-th power; $z, y_1, y_2$ in the level-$Nq$ function field, $u \in A$ and $w : \{0,1\} \to A$ are such that $(\bar v, \mathrm{red}\,u, z, y_1, y_2)$ forms a first-kind triple, that is either $(z, y_1, y_2) = (j, j_N, j_{Nq})$ with $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j - \mathrm{red}\,u) = 1$, or $(z, y_1, y_2) = (j_N, j, j_{Nq})$ with $\mathrm{ord}_{\bar v}(j_N - \mathrm{red}\,u) = 1$; and $z - u$ as well as each $y_j - w_j$ have positive order at $Q$. Finally let $g$ lie in the valuation subring `R.R₁.integers` of the first regular prolongation and be integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by `jFun N q`. Then there are multivariate polynomials $p, s$ in three variables indexed by `Option (Fin 2)` with coefficients in $A$ such that, evaluating via `evalBar` at the tuple $(z; y_1, y_2)$, one has $p(z, y_1, y_2) = g \cdot s(z, y_1, y_2)$ and $\mathrm{red}\bigl(s(u, w_0, w_1)\bigr) \neq 0$.
--
--   This is a Hartogs-type regularity statement for the three-coordinate model of $X_0(Nq)$: a function integral for the first Gauss prolongation and integral over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j]$ is a quotient of polynomials in the coordinates whose denominator does not reduce to zero at the chosen point, which expresses normality of the local ring of the model at that point. It is used in establishing the model property `IsModel` for smooth points of the first reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_exists_evalBar_eq_mul_evalBar_of_mem_integers_of_isIntegral.lean

